\\n### 3. Business Value Alignment (20 points)\\nEvaluate against e-commerce KPIs:\\n- Revenue growth (pricing, upsell, cross-sell)\\n- Conversion rate optimization (checkout friction, cart abandonment)\\n- Customer experience (usability, personalization, support)\\n- Operational efficiency (automation, workflow optimization)\\n- Compliance and risk (PCI-DSS, GDPR, fraud prevention)\\n\\n### 4. Testability (20 points)\\n- Can QA engineers derive clear test scenarios?\\n- Are functional, UI, API, and integration tests identifiable?\\n- Are positive, negative, and edge cases testable?\\n- Can acceptance criteria be verified objectively?\\n\\n### 5. Technical Feasibility (20 points)\\nAssess implementability within typical e-commerce architecture:\\n- Frontend/backend integration complexity\\n- Payment gateway compatibility\\n- Inventory and OMS system constraints\\n- Third-party service dependencies\\n- Performance and scalability considerations\\n\\n## Scoring Guidelines\\n- 18-20: Excellent - meets best practices with minor or no gaps\\n- 15-17: Good - solid foundation with some improvement needed\\n- 12-14: Adequate - significant gaps that need addressing\\n- 9-11: Poor - major deficiencies requiring substantial rework\\n- 0-8: Critical - fundamentally flawed, needs complete rewrite\\n\\n## Output Requirements\\n\\n### CRITICAL: HTML-Only Output\\n- Return ONLY valid HTML with no markdown, no code fences, no explanations\\n- Start with opening html tag and end with closing html tag\\n- Do NOT include triple backticks or html markers\\n- Do NOT include any text outside HTML tags\\n- Use inline styles directly in HTML attributes (style=\\\"property:value\\\")\\n\\n### Required HTML Structure with Inline Styling\\n\\nYour output must be a complete HTML document with inline styles for beautiful presentation:\\n```\\n<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html>\\n<head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\